    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class and it passes, with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the soft-duplicate flag on `POST /api/owners` with minimal structural impact \u2014 one small new function class, plus tiny additive edits.\n\n**What \"possible duplicate\" means:** a new owner that clears the hard-duplicate check (`CheckUniqueIdentity`) but still shares an existing owner's `lastName` (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed) and `postcode` while having a **different** telephone is still created, and reports `possibleDuplicate: true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matched owner's id. Otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`.\n\n**Changes (4 files):**\n1. **`FlagPossibleDuplicate.java`** (new) \u2014 a single-method OfficeFloor step. It reuses `CheckUniqueHousehold.normalize` for the lastName comparison and records the match by setting `possibleDuplicateOf` on the entity; unmatched leaves it null.\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added one `@Transient Integer possibleDuplicateOf` field (mirroring the existing transient `bulkSignupWarning`), its getter/setter, and a derived `isPossibleDuplicate()`. Transient is sufficient because the create and the follow-up GET share one persistence context (as `bulkSignupWarning` already relies on), so no schema/DDL changes were needed.\n3. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `flagPossibleDuplicate` step between `flagBulkSignup` and `save`, under the same transaction governance.\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the two readonly `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` properties to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them; MapStruct maps them automatically by name, so `OwnerMapper` was untouched.\n\nNo existing function bodies were grown \u2014 the behaviour lives in one cohesive new unit with zero surrounding complexity, and the entity edits are trivial accessors.",
